Lindar scripsit:

> This is a very interesting concept indeed. A parliamentary
> dictatorship whose election is based on effort put forth... Long reign
> King Uncle Robin!

When the Roman Republic got into Really Serious Trouble, the Senate
would pass a resolution "that the consuls shall see to it that the
State takes no harm."  That was their clue to appoint a Dictator,
against whose decrees there was no right of appeal.

His term expired after six months.

